<div class="bhd-page__keypoints" aria-label="Best Hydrate mission principles">
  <div><strong>Useful science</strong><span>Translate physiology into decisions people can understand, not technical language for its own sake.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Transparent claims</strong><span>State what is established, what is product-specific and what still belongs in research.</span></div>
  <div><strong>Practical access</strong><span>Design for real preparation, real environments and partnerships that can expand appropriate access.</span></div>
</div>

<section class="bhd-page__feature">
  <div>
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Mission</p>
    <h2>Make oral hydration easier to understand and easier to use well</h2>
    <p>Best Hydrate is building a company around the idea that good hydration should connect mechanism, formulation, behaviour and context. The immediate product matters, but so does the quality of the information around it: what the ingredients do, when electrolyte drinks may be useful, where ordinary water remains enough, and when medical guidance takes priority.</p>
    <p>That mission requires restraint as much as ambition. Better hydration education is not created by implying that everyone is dehydrated, every electrolyte drink is medically necessary or every plausible mechanism has already been proven as a product outcome.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__cards-section">
  <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Our values</p>
  <h2>Seven standards we want visible in the work</h2>
  <div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--4">
    <article><h3>Evidence before hype</h3><p>Use established evidence where it exists, label uncertainty honestly and strengthen claims only when evidence justifies it.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Clarity before complexity</h3><p>Explain the practical meaning first, then give readers a path into deeper physiology, formula rationale and references.</p></article>
    <article><h3>People before categories</h3><p>Athletes, workers, older adults, travellers and patients are not interchangeable segments. Context changes the hydration problem.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Utility before novelty</h3><p>New features, ingredients and partnerships should solve a real problem rather than exist only because they are marketable.</p></article>
  </div>
  <div class="bhd-page__cards bhd-page__cards--3" style="margin-top:1.35rem">
    <article><h3>Transparency before perfection</h3><p>Correct old wording, publish status clearly and let the public see the difference between current evidence and future ambition.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Access with context</h3><p>Humanitarian and clinical-development work must consider implementation, safety, WASH systems, local partners and appropriate standards.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Continuous improvement</h3><p>Treat formulation, research, communication and operations as systems that should become better as new evidence and feedback arrive.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__split">
  <div class="bhd-page__split-media">
    <img src="https://images.pexels.com/photos/36692089/pexels-photo-36692089.jpeg?auto=compress&cs=tinysrgb&w=1500" alt="Gloved researcher carefully pouring liquid into a measuring beaker" width="1500" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
  </div>
  <div class="bhd-page__split-copy">
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">What the values change</p>
    <h2>Values only matter if they constrain decisions</h2>
    <p>These principles affect how Best Hydrate builds the website, evaluates product language, chooses research questions and approaches partners. A collaboration that requires exaggerated claims is a poor fit. A research result that challenges an assumption should improve the company rather than be hidden. A humanitarian idea that ignores local infrastructure is incomplete, no matter how attractive it looks in a presentation.</p>
    <p>The same standard applies to ordinary customer communication: useful, understandable and proportionate to the evidence.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bhd-page__prose-grid">
  <article class="bhd-page__prose">
    <p class="bhd-page__kicker">Long-term direction</p>
    <h2>Build credibility that compounds</h2>
    <p>The strongest version of Best Hydrate is not defined by the loudest hydration claim. It is defined by whether customers, researchers, clinicians, athletes, retailers and implementation partners can understand what the company knows, what it sells, what it is studying and where it is going.</p>
    <p>That is why the public site is structured around separate Science, Solutions and Connect families. Each has a different job, and keeping those jobs distinct helps the company stay ambitious without confusing aspiration with evidence.</p>
  </article>
  <aside class="bhd-page__callout">
    <span class="bhd-page__callout-label">Operating test</span>
    <h3>Can we explain the decision without hiding the tradeoff?</h3>
    <p>If not, the decision probably needs more work.</p>
  </aside>
</section>

